<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta
      name="viewport"
      content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"
    />
    <title>Tret — A CLI tool that installs other CLI tools</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Tret installs CLI tools from their install scripts, records what each install changes in a bounded capture window, and removes them cleanly later. Free and open source for macOS and Linux."
    />
    <meta
      name="theme-color"
      content="#ffffff"
      media="(prefers-color-scheme: light)"
    />
    <meta
      name="theme-color"
      content="#000000"
      media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)"
    />
    <link
      rel="icon"
      href="data:image/svg+xml,<svg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 32 32'><text x='4' y='24' font-family='ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace' font-size='20' fill='%23c084fc'>&gt;_</text></svg>"
    />
    <style>
      :root {
        color-scheme: light dark;
        --font-sans:
          "Inter Variable", Inter, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, "Helvetica Neue", "Noto Sans", Arial,
          sans-serif, "Apple Color Emoji", "Segoe UI Emoji", "Segoe UI Symbol", "Noto Color Emoji";
        --font-mono: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, "Liberation Mono", "Courier New", monospace;
        --background: oklch(1 0 0);
        --foreground: oklch(0.145 0 0);
        --card: oklch(1 0 0);
        --card-foreground: oklch(0.145 0 0);
        --primary: oklch(0.205 0 0);
        --primary-foreground: oklch(0.985 0 0);
        --muted: oklch(0.97 0 0);
        --muted-foreground: oklch(0.556 0 0);
        --border: oklch(0.922 0 0);
        --ring: oklch(0.708 0 0);
      }

      @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
        :root {
          --background: oklch(0% 0 0);
          --foreground: oklch(100% 0 0);
          --card: oklch(0.145 0 0);
          --card-foreground: oklch(0.985 0 0);
          --primary: oklch(0.922 0 0);
          --primary-foreground: oklch(0.145 0 0);
          --muted: oklch(0.205 0 0);
          --muted-foreground: oklch(0.708 0 0);
          --border: oklch(1 0 0 / 10%);
          --ring: oklch(0.708 0 0);
          --accent: #c084fc;
        }
      }

      * {
        box-sizing: border-box;
      }

      html {
        -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%;
        line-height: 1.5;
        font-family: var(--font-sans);
      }

      body {
        margin: 0;
        background: var(--background);
        color: var(--foreground);
      }

      h1,
      h2,
      p,
      ul {
        margin: 0;
      }

      ul {
        padding: 0;
        list-style: none;
      }

      a {
        color: inherit;
        text-decoration: none;
      }

      a:focus-visible {
        outline: 2px solid var(--ring);
        outline-offset: 2px;
      }

      strong {
        font-weight: 600;
      }

      code {
        font-family: var(--font-mono);
      }

      .page {
        display: flex;
        min-height: 100vh;
        min-height: 100svh;
        flex-direction: column;
      }

      .page > main {
        flex: 1;
      }

      .site-header {
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: space-between;
        gap: 1rem;
        padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
      }

      .site-header nav ul {
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 0.25rem;
      }

      .wordmark {
        font-size: 0.875rem;
        line-height: 1.25rem;
        font-weight: 600;
      }

      .section {
        width: 100%;
        max-width: 48rem;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 3rem 1rem;
      }

      .section.hero {
        padding-top: 4rem;
        padding-bottom: 4rem;
      }

      h1 {
        font-size: 2.25rem;
        line-height: 1.11;
        font-weight: 800;
        letter-spacing: -0.025em;
        text-wrap: balance;
      }

      h2 {
        font-size: 1.875rem;
        line-height: 1.2;
        font-weight: 600;
        letter-spacing: -0.025em;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
        padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
      }

      p {
        line-height: 1.75rem;
      }

      .lead {
        max-width: 65ch;
        font-size: 1.25rem;
        line-height: 1.4;
        color: var(--muted-foreground);
      }

      .muted {
        font-size: 0.875rem;
        line-height: 1.25rem;
        color: var(--muted-foreground);
      }

      .center {
        display: block;
        text-align: center;
      }

      .mt-2 {
        margin-top: 0.5rem;
      }

      .mt-4 {
        margin-top: 1rem;
      }

      .mt-6 {
        margin-top: 1.5rem;
      }

      .text-link {
        text-decoration: underline;
        text-underline-offset: 2px;
      }

      .actions {
        display: flex;
        width: fit-content;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        gap: 0.5rem;
      }

      .btn {
        display: inline-flex;
        flex-shrink: 0;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
        gap: 0.375rem;
        height: 2rem;
        padding: 0 0.625rem;
        border: 1px solid transparent;
        border-radius: 0;
        background-clip: padding-box;
        font-size: 0.75rem;
        line-height: 1rem;
        font-weight: 500;
        white-space: nowrap;
        transition: all 0.15s cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1);
        outline: none;
        user-select: none;
        cursor: pointer;
      }

      .btn:focus-visible {
        border-color: var(--ring);
        box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px color-mix(in oklab, var(--ring) 50%, transparent);
      }

      .btn:active {
        transform: translateY(1px);
      }

      .btn-primary {
        background: var(--primary);
        color: var(--primary-foreground);
      }

      .btn-primary:hover {
        background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--primary) 80%, transparent);
      }

      .btn-outline {
        border-color: var(--border);
        background: var(--background);
        color: var(--foreground);
      }

      .btn-outline:hover,
      .btn-ghost:hover {
        background: var(--muted);
        color: var(--foreground);
      }

      .code {
        display: flex;
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        background: var(--muted);
        font-family: var(--font-mono);
        font-size: 0.75rem;
        line-height: 1.4;
      }

      .code code {
        flex: 1;
        min-width: 0;
        padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
        white-space: pre;
        overflow-x: auto;
      }

      .code .prompt {
        color: var(--muted-foreground);
        user-select: none;
      }

      @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
        .code .prompt {
          color: var(--accent);
        }
      }

      .code-copy {
        flex-shrink: 0;
        min-width: 5rem;
        padding: 0 1rem;
        border: 0;
        border-left: 1px solid var(--border);
        background: transparent;
        color: var(--muted-foreground);
        font: inherit;
        cursor: pointer;
        transition: color 0.15s cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1);
      }

      .code-copy:hover {
        color: var(--foreground);
      }

      .code-copy:focus-visible {
        outline: 2px solid var(--ring);
        outline-offset: -2px;
      }

      .grid {
        display: grid;
        gap: 1rem;
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }

      @media (min-width: 640px) {
        .grid {
          grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
        }
      }

      .card {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 0.25rem;
        padding: 1rem;
        background: var(--card);
        color: var(--card-foreground);
        box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px color-mix(in oklab, var(--foreground) 10%, transparent);
        font-size: 0.75rem;
        line-height: 1.625;
      }

      .card-title {
        font-size: 0.875rem;
        line-height: 1.25rem;
        font-weight: 500;
      }

      .card-desc {
        color: var(--muted-foreground);
      }

      .card-meta {
        font-family: var(--font-mono);
        font-size: 0.75rem;
        line-height: 1rem;
        color: var(--muted-foreground);
      }

      .site-footer {
        padding: 1.5rem 1rem;
      }

      .separator {
        height: 1px;
        width: 100%;
        margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
        background: var(--border);
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="page">
      <header class="site-header">
        <a
          class="wordmark"
          href="/"
          >Tret</a
        >
        <nav aria-label="Main">
          <ul>
            <li>
              <a
                class="btn btn-ghost"
                href="https://github.com/framwrk/tret"
                >GitHub</a
              >
            </li>
          </ul>
        </nav>
      </header>
      <main>
        <section class="section hero">
          <h1>Tret</h1>
          <p class="lead mt-4">A CLI tool that installs other CLI tools.</p>
          <p class="mt-6">
            Tret runs a tool's installer inside a bounded capture window, records what it creates, overwrites, or deletes
            there, and uninstalls cleanly later — a path is touched only while its recorded fingerprint still matches.
          </p>
          <div class="code mt-6">
            <code><span class="prompt">$ </span>curl -fsSL https://tret.framwrk.com/scripts/install.sh | bash</code>
            <button
              type="button"
              class="code-copy"
            >
              Copy
            </button>
          </div>
          <p class="muted mt-4">
            Installs the latest release to <code>~/.tret/bin</code> and links it as <code>~/.local/bin/tret</code>, after
            verifying it against the published checksums. Update in place with <code>tret update</code>, or a tracked tool with
            <code>tret update &lt;tool&gt;</code>.
          </p>
          <div class="actions mt-6">
            <a
              class="btn btn-primary"
              href="https://github.com/framwrk/tret"
              >View on GitHub</a
            >
            <a
              class="btn btn-outline"
              href="https://github.com/framwrk/tret/releases"
              >Releases</a
            >
          </div>
        </section>
        <section class="section">
          <h2>What it does</h2>
          <div class="grid mt-6">
            <div class="card">
              <div class="card-title">Install</div>
              <div class="card-desc">
                Fetches the install script, shows its hash and a preview, runs it in a bounded capture window, and records the
                files it changed.
              </div>
              <div class="card-meta mt-2">tret install &lt;URL&gt;</div>
            </div>
            <div class="card">
              <div class="card-title">Uninstall</div>
              <div class="card-desc">
                Removes owned files and symlinks only while their recorded fingerprints match; divergent paths are kept.
              </div>
              <div class="card-meta mt-2">tret uninstall &lt;tool&gt;</div>
            </div>
            <div class="card">
              <div class="card-title">Inspect</div>
              <div class="card-desc">
                Shows a record without changing anything: capture confidence, owned paths, files changed since install, and what
                uninstall would do.
              </div>
              <div class="card-meta mt-2">tret inspect &lt;tool&gt;</div>
            </div>
            <div class="card">
              <div class="card-title">Trace</div>
              <div class="card-desc">
                Runs a tracked tool in a bounded observation window and appends what it writes as a separate segment. Opt-in,
                never silent.
              </div>
              <div class="card-meta mt-2">tret trace &lt;tool&gt;</div>
            </div>
            <div class="card">
              <div class="card-title">Update</div>
              <div class="card-desc">
                Updates Tret itself, or re-runs a tracked tool's recorded installer with its original arguments.
              </div>
              <div class="card-meta mt-2">tret update [tool]</div>
            </div>
            <div class="card">
              <div class="card-title">Track</div>
              <div class="card-desc">
                Lists captured tools, adopts commands you installed yourself, and can stop tracking without touching files.
              </div>
              <div class="card-meta mt-2">tret list · tret find · tret forget</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="muted mt-4">
            Most commands accept <code>--json</code> for one machine-readable document, with stable exit codes for scripts and
            CI.
          </p>
          <p class="muted mt-4">
            Capture is bounded and labeled, not a full filesystem diff: macOS uses a scoped heuristic snapshot with no process
            attribution, and a Linux window is <code>complete</code> only when the traced process tree was fully observed.
            <code>tret inspect</code> shows what a record actually covers, and the
            <a
              class="text-link"
              href="https://github.com/framwrk/tret#capture-coverage-and-limits"
              >capture limits</a
            >
            are documented in the README.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section class="section">
          <h2>Platform support</h2>
          <p class="mt-4">macOS and Linux, on both arm64 and x64. Windows is not supported.</p>
          <p class="muted mt-4">
            Prefer to read before you run? The install and uninstall scripts are plain shell. Read
            <a
              class="text-link"
              href="https://github.com/framwrk/tret/blob/main/scripts/install.sh"
              >install.sh</a
            >
            and
            <a
              class="text-link"
              href="https://github.com/framwrk/tret/blob/main/scripts/uninstall.sh"
              >uninstall.sh</a
            >
            in the repo.
          </p>
        </section>
      </main>
      <footer class="site-footer">
        <div class="separator"></div>
        <p class="muted center">© 2026 Framwrk. All rights reserved.</p>
      </footer>
    </div>
    <script>
      for (const box of document.querySelectorAll(".code")) {
        const code = box.querySelector("code");
        const button = box.querySelector(".code-copy");
        button.addEventListener("click", async () => {
          const command = code.cloneNode(true);
          command.querySelector(".prompt")?.remove();
          try {
            await navigator.clipboard.writeText(command.textContent);
            button.textContent = "Copied";
            setTimeout(() => (button.textContent = "Copy"), 1500);
          } catch {
            // Clipboard access can be denied; the command stays selectable by hand.
          }
        });
      }
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
